A||||28||burdell1||cup holders||||||
Z||000000||burdell1||07-23-99||01:13 PM||||Has anyone out there thought of some unique places to put cup holders in their Fiero? 
Z||000001||G25C||07-23-99||10:05 PM||||When i bought my 87 GT, somebody had taken one of those single cup holder (the kind that has a flat hook shape to attached to the top and is soposed to flip over the door panel of most cars and trucks and hang from there).  But the flattend out the "hook" part and slid it between the space that seperates the rally guages from the radio/heater pannel, on the passenger side.  I can still remove it and it fits in there pretty tight.  (It has no problem holding McDonalds new large size cup and doesnt let it tip either).  And there was no special alterations to do before putting it there.  <p>I you want to show your Fiero just pull it back out.<p>Now, im not so sure that this is a good place for a drink holder, being that maybe somehow it applies pressure from the wait of the cup to the upper guages area.  But its been there quite awhile and i have no problems with the function of my guages and no stress marks on the interior where its attached.<p>And if the drink sweats, the drops hit the floor mat and nothing else.<p>I think that its a great place for it, however if someone knows of a reason that i should not put it there. Please tell me and ill remove it immiediatly.<p>(as for the place for a second drink holder for the passenger?  Well, they can just hold on to theres...besides, there not doing the driving!).<p> 
Z||000002||lowCG||07-24-99||12:11 AM||||I was at the VW dealer a few years back,and the '95 Passats had an optional holder that mounted to the trans tunnel,on the side,down low.It folded up nice and tight to the tunnel when not in use,real nice part also(well made).
Z||000003||GREENDANO||07-24-99||07:10 AM||||I usually buy the 32-48 ounce "Big Gulp"  The plastic cup will slide down in the cavity/space to the right and rear of the instrument cluster.  Try it, it works!  But only with certain size cups, plus I guess if you're a coffee drinker, (i'm not) I don't think 48 onces of coffee in you would be good for the people around who will have to put up with you.<br>  Dan-O
Z||000004||Pretender||07-24-99||05:25 PM||||well one morning after work i went to mcdonalds and got a super size orange juice(biggest cup they have). when i got into my car i sat it over the powermirror switch. i went to put the car in reverse(auto) and my elbo knocked it over and before i could catch it the cup was empty!!!...think i wasn't about to cry..it took me 4 hours to tear apart the interior and shampoo the carpets.....with that all done i will never DRINK and DRIVE again..*S*..i've seen a new interior that has cup holders molded in but it costs about $1,000...i will buy it when i get everything else done to the car...:o)
Z||000005||Gokart||07-24-99||07:43 PM||||I put one in I bought at Walmart! It's adjustable and I mounted it on the right hand side of the radio console with short screws. I don't like to put holes in anything in my Fiero, but I figure it's my car and will NEVER be anyone elses, so I put in what works for me!
Z||000006||Formula||07-24-99||07:49 PM||||I took the speaker out of the dash and made a nice cup holder. Now I just use a long straw. 
Z||000007||Patrick||07-24-99||08:01 PM||||<br>Well, I made a custom holder that sits over the spare tire and I use a <b>really</b> long straw.<p>The heat from the radiator helps to keep my coffee hot too. Now if I could just figure out a way to keep slurpees from melting so fast... <IMG SRC="http://www.compucheap.com/ubb/smile.gif"> <p>
Z||000008||Racer 1||07-25-99||02:19 AM||||You guys crack me up.I have found one cupholder item that will fit everywhere.Its one of the baseball plastic hats you wear with the two cup holders on each side with the two straws coming down to you mouth.Then you could put a big fiero emblim on the hat in the front.You would be shag-a-dellict!!OR you could use a camelpack and have it on your chest instead of your back then if you ever got in a wreck it would act like a airbag and then it would cool ya down while your engine catches fire!!!
Z||000009||DJRice||07-26-99||11:30 AM||||I just stick a really long straw <b>in</b> the radiator.....<p>With the seats all the way back I usually just wedge my drink between the seat and the upper part of the console.  That seems to work well.  
Z||000010||theogre||07-26-99||11:51 AM||||I just said the hell with washing the windscreen and hooked the washer tank up IV. Nothing like the direct injection of a gallon of coffee first thing in the morning to get you off to work.....<br>
Z||000011||lowCG||07-26-99||12:04 PM||||Oh no,The Ogre's got me thinking again;how about an espresso made with the blow-off pressure from the radiator,would have to re-load daily,and make sure and remember your mug.
