Z||000014||Phil||09-10-1999||02:52 PM||||Went to West Marine  and found fold-up cup holders. They measure 4 1/4 " square and are about 1/2" thick when folded. I put one on the inst.pod by the trunk release switch and the other on the side of the radio console. Looks like they came from the factory and they only cost $5.00 each||||reg||
Z||000015||Kage86GT4SP||09-11-1999||01:10 AM||||For my 52 oz insulated cup (I got mine at a 7-11, I recommend it because it keeps my diet coke colder for a lot longer then the non-insulated, thin plastic variety... so I toss out a lot less.  It actually saves money in the long-run), it fits perfectly to the left of the instrument panel and the door.<P>I tank it up every morning on the way to work, along with a 34 oz coffee.  The coffee fits in a cup-holder that's held in place by the seat back of the pass. seat... there's a long, wavy piece of plastic about 10 inches by 4 wide that slips under the seat back when you bend it forward, and locks it into place when you put the seat into the upright<BR>position.  I got that one out of an AM-PM.<P><BR>Enjoy!||||reg||1
Z||000016||DISenchanted||09-13-1999||04:55 PM||||I'm working on a set of cup holders that will resemble the fold out one located on the newer style camaro's (97-), they should be ready in about 2 weeks.  I'll post a picture soon.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Phil||01-05-2000||07:14 PM||||Here's a shot of my marine store cup holders:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cupholder.jpg"> ||||reg||3
Z||000018||Ed||01-05-2000||09:54 PM||||For "Slurpee" drinkers: Many years ago I read about a way to keep a six-pack cold. Get a small, disposable stryrofoam cooler and open up one side and put it next to your air conditioner accumulator. The accumulator is cold when your air is on.  ||||reg||1
