Z||000022||bHooper||04-27-2000||04:10 PM||||<B>NOT</B> haveing a cup holder is one of the little luxuries of Fiero ownership!  Besides, it gives everyone else something else to complain about  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I like it that way.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000023||Gold-86SE||04-27-2000||05:41 PM||||The way I see it.<P>The Fiero is one of the last great cars of the Eighties.  Made before the mass populas(sp) decided that they needed cup holders, dual cig lighters and all the rest of the "convience items."<P>If you drive and push the Fiero for maximum excitement you will not want a cup holder, because you will not have a drink. Your left hand is on the wheel, the right hand on the shifter, and you're driving that thing for all she's worth.<P>Who really, honestly, needs and wants a cup holder anyway, soccer moms/dads?<P>I say long live the non-cup holder.<P><BR>As a footnote, don't flame me if you disagree because this was IMHO.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000024||KnightRyder31||04-27-2000||06:33 PM||||I totaly agree with you GOLD-86, I love to drive my Fiero to the limit, while still babying her. I could not possibly have a cup holder in my car, because whenever I would be driving, my drink would be on my lap! I love my fiero just the way she is! The Fiero is the best caar I have ever owned. I think we are all privilaged to own one of the best. <BR>Knight||||reg||1
